On Sun, 13 Aug 2006 12:22:53 -0700, angelomcm wrote:

> Hi,
> By upgrading my windows version from W2K to XP, I have noticed my
> MS-DOS
> version of nethack (the one i like due to the full-screen option)
> decided to switch to the
> QWERTY keyboard-layout instead of my keyboard-native AZERTY layout.
> 
> I have checked the default options, but did not found a solution.
> Can somebody guide me to a quick fix or solution for this minor problem
> ?

In your defaults.nh file, look for this line:

# OPTIONS=altkeyhandler:nhraykey.dll

and uncomment it; this DLL is meant to deal with non-USA keyboards.

And read up on bug W343-4, for which I humbly apologize.  You might try
searching Google Groups for "nhraykey" for more details; it's nothing
fatal, but may be irritating for some users.


